    rdfs:seeAlso <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ordovician> ;
    skos:definition "Prior to revision of the Ordovician series and stages in the type area of England and Wales by Fortey et al. (1995), the top of the Llanvirn Series was considered to be at a lower stratigraphic level, approximating to the top of the modern Abereiddian Stage. This is now a deprecated definition of the Llanvirn Series, approximately equating to the modern Abereiddian Stage (Fortey et al., 1995, fig. 1)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme geochronology:Division ;
