    rdfs:seeAlso <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Weichselian> ;
    skos:broader division:QPL ;
    skos:definition "Weichselian Stage is the last Late Pleistocene stage in the NW European Quaternary climatostratigraphic scheme. It is interpreted as a cold (glacial) interval. It is preceded by the Eemian Stage. It is contemporaneous with the Devensian Stage in Great Britain (Geologic Time Scale 2020, fig. 30.2; BGS Research Report RR/10/003, table 1b)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme geochronology:Division ;
    skos:notation "BD"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Weichselian Stage"@en ;
.

