    rdfs:seeAlso <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eemian> ;
    skos:broader division:QPL ;
    skos:definition "Eemian Stage is a Late Pleistocene stage in the NW European Quaternary climatostratigraphic scheme. It is interpreted as a temporate (interglacial) interval. It is preceded by the Saalian Stage and succeeded by the Weichselian Stage. It is contemporaneous with the Ipswichian Stage in Great Britain, and with Marine Isotope Stage 5e (Geologic Time Scale 2020, fig. 30.2; BGS Research Report RR/10/003, table 1b)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme geochronology:Division ;
    skos:notation "BI"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Eemian Stage"@en ;
