    skos:broader division:BT ;
    skos:definition "Tiglian Substage B is an Early Pleistocene substage in the NW European Quaternary climatostratigraphic scheme. It is the second of three substages within the Tiglian Stage. It is preceded by Tiglian Substage A, and succeeded by Tiglian Substage C. It is contemporaneous with the Thurnian Stage in Great Britain (BGS Research Report RR/10/003, table 1b)."@en ;
