    skos:broader division:BT ;
    skos:definition "Tiglian Substage C is an Early Pleistocene substage in the NW European Quaternary climatostratigraphic scheme. It is the last of three substages within the Tiglian Stage. It is preceded by Tiglian Substage B. It is contemporaneous with the Antian/Bramertonian-to-Pastonian stages in Great Britain (BGS Research Report RR/10/003, table 1b)."@en ;
