    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:broader division:QD ;
    skos:definition "Windermere Interstadial is a relatively warm period near the end of the Devensian Stage. It is preceded by the Dimlington Stadial and succeeded by the Loch Lomond Stadial (BGS Research Report RR/10/003, table 1b; BGS British Regional Geology: Northern England (Fifth edition), fig. 64)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme geochronology:Division ;
    skos:notation "QDW"@en ;
